Hello!

I asked for the location of VMS GNU emacs binaries.  As I was informed
by several kind folks, GNU FAQ file answers my question; I just did
not think of looking there (I asked archie and also I looked in Emacs
distribution). To wit, here's question 105:

 Where do I get Emacs that runs on VMS under DECwindows?
  
  Hal R. Brand <BRAND@addvax.llnl.gov> is said to have a VMS save set with a
  ready-to-run VMS version of Emacs 18.55 for X Windows.  It is available
  via anonymous FTP (addvax.llnl.gov).  It is possible that the VMS versions
  of Emacs at other sites have X support compiled in.  See etc/FTP for
  locations.

As James A. McLaughlin <mclaughlin@asc.slb.com> writes, Hal's version
(derived from 18.55) has support for DECwindows and Rmail, among other
things not available from the one distributed by FSF. There also is a
non-DECwindows executable, and bunch of interesting X programs ported
to vms, most interestingly including Xterm (with its TEK emulation,
missing in dxterm), as well as xsnap, xgif, xwps and xfish.

 This site is running VMS, so an anonymous ftp from a conforming VMS
TCP/IP program (mine was CMU) will transfer files in correct record
format/size.

Thanks again to all respondents.

		przemek
