Hello!

We are running programs that control the external hardware. The same
program is used to (1) actually change the functions executed, and (2)
to look up the current data/status/etc. We want to keep (1) a
privileged operation, to be executed only from terminals that are
physically close to the hardware (for safety reasons), while (2) can
be executed from any local terminal. Currently, the instrument terminals are
hooked up to dedicated serial lines, so it is easy to look up the port
number and grant privileges based on that.

However, we want to move to LAT and network (DECWindows) terminals; my 2 questions
are:
 - is there a way to tell (from within a program) which terminal is logged over a LAT? 
   (LAT/Port pair would of course identify the terminal uniquely) I expect this to be 
   easy, it is just that we don't have much experience with LAT.
 - is there a way to tell (from within a program) which DECWindow terminal (DECnet 
   transport) is being used (the Ethernet address or DECnet node name/number will
   do the trick)

Anyone who could answer either question (or both) would gain our gratitude. Please
either e-mail or follow up; I will summarize .

